<script>
var S1='<svg viewBox="0 0 300 178" width="100%" style="max-width:430px">',S2='</svg>',D=[[0,1,"The magnitude of the vector A = 3î − 4ĵ is",["√7","5","7","1"],1,"|A| = √(3² + (−4)²) = √25 = 5;Component ka negative nishaan square me khatam ho jaata hai;Magnitude hamesha positive hota hai, isliye −5 kabhi nahi.",7],[0,1,"For the scalars p = 5 and q = −2, the values of p + q and p · q are respectively",["3 and −7","10 and 3","3 and −10","−7 and −10"],2,"Scalar me keval sankhya hoti hai, disha nahi;Addition: p + q = 5 + (−2) = 3;Multiplication: p · q = 5 × (−2) = −10, nishaan badal jaata hai.",-1],[0,1,"Which of the following is NOT a unit vector",["î","0.6î + 0.8ĵ","−ĵ","î + ĵ"],3,"Unit vector ka magnitude exactly 1 hona chahiye;|î + ĵ| = √(1 + 1) = √2 ≠ 1, atah yeh unit vector nahi;|0.6î + 0.8ĵ| = √(0.36 + 0.64) = 1 ✓;kisi bhi vector ko uske magnitude se divide karne se unit vector ban jaata hai.",-1],[0,1,"If |A| = 3, |B| = 4 and A · B = 6, the angle between the two vectors is",["60°","30°","90°","45°"],0,"Definition A · B = AB cosθ se cosθ = {6~12} = 0.5;θ = cos⁻¹(0.5) = 60°;Dot product ka result scalar hota hai — keval sankhya, disha nahi.",-1],[0,1,"If A = 2î + 3ĵ + x k̂ and B = î − 2ĵ + 4 k̂ are perpendicular to each other, then x equals",["−1","1","2","0"],1,"Perpendicular ka arth A · B = 0;Components ka product jodo: 2(1) + 3(−2) + x(4) = 0;2 − 6 + 4x = 0 se x = 1;do vectors perpendicular ho sakte hain bina zero bane — yahi dot product ki khaasiyat hai.",-1],[0,1,"If |A| = 3, |B| = 4 and the angle between them is 30°, then the magnitude |A × B| equals",["6√3","3","6","12"],2,"Formula |A × B| = AB sinθ = 3 × 4 × sin 30°;sin 30° = {1~2}, atah magnitude = 6;12 tab milta agar sin 30° ki jagah 1 rakh dete;direction plane ke normal par hoti hai (right-hand rule).",-1],[0,2,"If A · (B × C) = 5, then the value of (A × B) · C is",["−5","0","25","5"],3,"Scalar triple product cyclic order me aprivaartit rehta hai: A · (B × C) = B · (C × A) = C · (A × B);iskar (A × B) · C = 5;koi do vectors aapas me swap karo to keval nishaan badalta hai.",-1],[0,2,"For two non-zero vectors, the two conditions A · B = 0 and A × B = 0 cannot hold simultaneously. The reason is",["The two conditions are contradictory","They hold at θ = 0°","They hold at θ = 90°","They hold when A = B"],0,"A · B = AB cosθ = 0 se cosθ = 0, yaani θ = 90°;A × B = AB sinθ = 0 se sinθ = 0, yaani θ = 0° ya 180°;ek hi angle dono shartein poori nahi kar sakta, atah dono conditions virodhi hain.",-1],[0,1,"The magnitude of the resultant of the displacements d₁ = 2î + 3ĵ, d₂ = −î + ĵ and d₃ = 4î − 3ĵ, in metres, is",["7","√26 ≈ 5.1","13","√193"],1,"Same axis ke components alag-alag jodo: Rₓ = 2 − 1 + 4 = 5, R_y = 3 + 1 − 3 = 1;|R| = √(5² + 1²) = √26 ≈ 5.1 m;13 m keval tab aata hai jab teeno displacements ek hi line me hon.",-1],[1,1,"If y = x³ + 5x, then {dy~dx} equals",["x² + 5","3x + 5","3x² + 5","3x² + 5x"],2,"Power rule {d~dx} xⁿ = nx^(n−1) ko har pad par alag-alag lagu karo;{d(x³)~dx} = 3x² aur {d(5x)~dx} = 5;uttar 3x² + 5 — 5, x se guna hone wala constant hai, isliye derivative me bacha rehta hai.",-1],[1,1,"The derivative {d(√x)~dx} is equal to",["2√x","{1~√x}","{√x~2}","{1~2√x}"],3,"√x ko x^({1~2}) roop me likho;power rule se {1~2}x^(−{1~2}) = {1~2√x};x = 0 par yeh infinite ho jaata hai, kyunki vahaan curve vertical (y-axis ko sparsh) ho jaata hai.",-1],[1,2,"Differentiate x² sin x with respect to x.",["2x sin x + x² cos x","2x cos x","x² cos x","2x sin x − x² cos x"],0,"Product rule lagao: (uv)′ = u′v + uv′;yahaan u = x², u′ = 2x, v = sin x, v′ = cos x;uttar 2x sin x + x² cos x — dono pad plus me jodte hain, minus nahi aata.",-1],[1,1,"The derivative {dv~dx} of the function v = {x~x²} is",["ln x","−{1~x²}","{1~x²}","2x"],1,"Pehle cancel karke simplify karo: {x~x²} = {1~x} = x⁻¹;derivative = −1 · x⁻² = −{1~x²};quotient rule se bhi wahi milta hai, par pehle simplify karna tez aur galti-rahit hai.",-1],[1,2,"If u = sin 3x, then {du~dx} is",["−3 cos 3x","3 sin 3x","3 cos 3x","cos 3x"],2,"Chain rule: bahar wale ka derivative cos 3x, andar wale 3x ka derivative 3;dono ko guna karo: 3 cos 3x;keval cos 3x likh dena sabse common pariksha-truti hai.",-1],[1,2,"The slope of the curve y = e^(2x) at the point x = 0 is",["1","e²","0","2"],3,"{dy~dx} = 2e^(2x) — chain rule ka factor 2 bahar aata hai;x = 0 rakhne par 2e⁰ = 2 × 1 = 2;slope ka arth tanα, jahaan α tangent ka x-axis se bana angle hai.",-1],[1,1,"{d~dx} ln 5x equals",["{1~x}","{5~x}","{1~5x}","ln 5"],0,"Log ka rule: ln 5x = ln 5 + ln x;ln 5 ek constant hai, iska derivative zero;bachta hai {1~x} — log ke andar ka constant factor slope nahi badalta.",-1],[1,3,"If y = x^(-2) cos x, then {dy~dx} is",["x^(-2) sin x","−2x^(-3) cos x − x^(-2) sin x","2x^(-1) sin x","−2x^(-3) cos x + x^(-2) sin x"],1,"Product rule: u = x^(-2) aur v = cos x;u′ = −2x^(-3), v′ = −sin x;uttar −2x^(-3) cos x − x^(-2) sin x;donon pad negative hain kyonki x badhne par dono factors ghatte hain.",-1],[1,3,"If x = t² and y = t³, then {dy~dx} equals",["3t²","2t","{3t~2}","{2t~3}"],2,"Parametric rule: {dy~dx} = {dy~dt} ÷ {dx~dt};{dy~dt} = 3t² aur {dx~dt} = 2t;anupat {3t²~2t} = {3t~2};t = 0 par dono derivatives zero hain, vahaan yeh vidhi kaam nahi karti.",-1],[1,2,"For a displacement given by x = A sin ωt, the acceleration is",["ω²x","−Aω sin ωt","ω²A sin ωt","−ω²x"],3,"v = {dx~dt} = Aω cos ωt;phir a = {dv~dt} = −Aω² sin ωt;kyonki x = A sin ωt, atah a = −ω²x;acceleration, displacement ke samanupati aur uske viparit disha me — yahi SHM ki paribhasha hai.",-1],[1,2,"If f(t) = (3t² + 1)(2t − 1), then f′(t) is",["18t² − 6t + 2","6t² + 2","12t","18t² + 2"],0,"Product rule: (6t)(2t − 1) + (3t² + 1)(2);brackets kholo: 12t² − 6t + 6t² + 2;jodne par 18t² − 6t + 2;pehle brackets kholkar differentiate karke bhi yahi check kar sakte ho.",-1],[1,3,"{d~dx} ln(cos x) equals",["−cot x","−tan x","tan x","sec x"],1,"Chain rule: {d~du} ln u = {1~u}, yahaan u = cos x;{du~dx} = −sin x, atah {1~cos x} × (−sin x);uttar −tan x — andar ka function ghat raha hai, isliye nishaan negative.",-1],[1,2,"{d~dx} {x + 1~x − 1} equals",["{1~x² − 1}","{2x~(x − 1)²}","−{2~(x − 1)²}","{2~(x − 1)²}"],2,"Quotient rule me numerator: (1)(x − 1) − (x + 1)(1) = −2;denominator = (x − 1)², jo hamesha positive hai;uttar −{2~(x − 1)²} — nishaan ka faisala sirf numerator karta hai.",-1],[1,2,"Differentiate x eˣ with respect to x.",["x eˣ","eˣ","eˣ(x − 1)","eˣ(1 + x)"],3,"Product rule: (x)′eˣ + x(eˣ)′ = eˣ + x eˣ;eˣ common lo: eˣ(1 + x);yahi identity aage ∫ eˣ(1 + x)dx = x eˣ + C ban jaati hai.",-1],[2,1,"∫ x² dx equals",["{x³~3} + C","2x + C","x³ + C","{x²~2} + C"],0,"Rule ∫ xⁿdx = {xⁿ⁺¹~n + 1} + C me n = 2 rakho;uttar {x³~3} + C;janch: {d~dx}{x³~3} = x² ✓;2x + C to derivative ka answer hai, integral ka nahi.",-1],[2,1,"∫₁² {dx~x²} equals",["−{1~2}","{1~2}","1","ln 2"],1,"x⁻² ka antiderivative = −x⁻¹ = −{1~x};upper limit par −{1~2}, lower limit par −1;difference = −{1~2} − (−1) = {1~2};ln 2 tab aata jab integrand {1~x} hota.",-1],[2,2,"∫_(0)^(π) sin x dx equals",["1","π","2","0"],2,"∫ sin x dx = −cos x (minus ka dhyan rakho);limits: (−cos π) − (−cos 0) = 1 + 1;uttar 2, kyonki 0 se π tak curve positive hai;π se 2π tak isi ka value −2 aayega.",-1],[2,2,"∫ cos ax dx, where a is a non-zero constant, equals",["−{sin(ax)~a} + C","a sin(ax) + C","{cos(ax)~a} + C","{sin(ax)~a} + C"],3,"Andar ka constant a divide karke bahar aa jaata hai: {sin(ax)~a} + C;janch karo: {d~dx}{sin(ax)~a} = cos(ax) ✓;a se guna karna (a sin ax) truti hai.",-1],[2,3,"∫_(0)^(a) {dx~√(a² − x²)} equals",["{π~2}","1","sin⁻¹ a","π"],0,"Standard form: ∫ {dx~√(a² − x²)} = sin⁻¹{x~a};limits: sin⁻¹{a~a} − sin⁻¹0 = sin⁻¹1 − 0;uttar {π~2}. x = a par integrand infinite ho jaata hai, phir bhi kshetraphal simit hai.",-1],[2,2,"∫₀¹ eˣ dx equals",["ln 2","e − 1","1","e"],1,"eˣ ka antiderivative svayan eˣ hota hai;limits: e¹ − e⁰ = e − 1 ≈ 1.718;e⁰ = 1 ghatana bhoolne par galat option 'e' dikhega — wahi trap yahaan rakha gaya hai.",6],[2,2,"∫₋ₐᵃ x³ dx equals",["a⁴","−a⁴","0","{2a⁴~4}"],2,"x³ ek odd function hai, arthaat f(−x) = −f(x);origin ke donon taraf ke kshetraphal same magnitude par opposite nishaan ke hote hain, atah yog zero;even function (x² ya |x|) me value double ho jaati.",-1],[2,3,"∫ {x dx~x² + 1} equals",["ln(x² + 1) + C","tan⁻¹ x + C","{x²~2} ln(x² + 1) + C","{1~2} ln(x² + 1) + C"],3,"Put u = x² + 1, tab du = 2x dx, arthaat x dx = {du~2};integral = {1~2}∫ {du~u} = {1~2} ln(x² + 1) + C;jab denominator ka derivative numerator me maujood ho, substitution sabse tez marg hai.",-1],[2,3,"∫ {dx~√(1 − x²)} equals",["sin⁻¹ x + C","ln(1 − x²) + C","cos⁻¹ x + C","tan⁻¹ x + C"],0,"Smaran rakho: {d~dx} sin⁻¹x = {1~√(1 − x²)};atah uttar sin⁻¹x + C;cos⁻¹x ka derivative negative aata hai;denominator me 1 + x² hota to tan⁻¹x milta — keval nishaan ka farak hai.",-1],[2,3,"∫_(0)^(∞) e^({−t~τ}) dt equals",["τ²","τ","1","0"],1,"Antiderivative = −τe^({−t~τ}) — τ uthakar bahar aa jaata hai;upper limit t → ∞ par value 0;lower limit t = 0 par value −τ;uttar 0 − (−τ) = τ, isiliye τ ko kul kshetraphal kahte hain.",4],[2,2,"The solution of the differential equation {dN~dt} = −λN is",["N = N₀ − λt","N = {N₀~λt}","N = N₀e^(−λt)","N = N₀e^(λt)"],2,"Chal-pṛthakkaran: {dN~N} = −λ dt;donon taraf integrate: ln N = −λt + C;initial condition t = 0, N = N₀ se C = ln N₀;uttar N = N₀e^(−λt) — negative exponent kshay dikhata hai.",4],[2,2,"∫₁ᵉ {dx~x} equals",["e","0","ln 2","1"],3,"∫ {dx~x} = ln x;limits: ln e − ln 1 = 1 − 0 = 1;yahi curve y = {1~x} ke neeche x = 1 se x = e tak ka kshetraphal hai — natural logarithm ki zyamiitiyak paribhasha.",3],[2,3,"∫₁² (2t + 3) dt equals",["6","8","10","5"],0,"Antiderivative: t² + 3t;upper limit t = 2 par 4 + 6 = 10;lower limit t = 1 par 1 + 3 = 4;uttar 10 − 4 = 6 — keval 10 likh dena common galti hai.",-1],[2,3,"{d~dx} ∫₀ˣ t² dt equals",["0","x²","{x³~3}","2x"],1,"Kalan ke maulik pryay se: {d~dx} ∫ₐˣ f(t)dt = f(x);yahaan f(t) = t², atah seedha uttar x²;pehle integrate karke phir derivative lena vyarth mehnat hai, aur constant bhi zero hi aayega.",-1],[2,2,"∫₀¹ {dx~1 + x²} equals",["1","{π~2}","{π~4}","ln 2"],2,"Standard integral: ∫ {dx~1 + x²} = tan⁻¹x + C;limits: tan⁻¹1 − tan⁻¹0 = {π~4} − 0;denominator me 1 − x² hota to {1~2}ln{1 + x~1 − x} jaisa roop milta.",-1],[2,2,"∫ eˣ(1 + x) dx equals",["eˣ + C","(1 + x)eˣ + C","{eˣ~1 + x} + C","x eˣ + C"],3,"Pehchan lo: ∫ eˣ[f(x) + f′(x)]dx = eˣ f(x) + C;yahaan f = x aur f′ = 1, jo integrand se bilkul mel khaata hai;uttar x eˣ + C (by-parts se bhi wahi, par pehchan tez hai).",-1],[2,3,"The value of ∫₀² (3x² − 2) dx is",["4","0","8","2"],0,"Antiderivative: x³ − 2x;upper limit x = 2 par 8 − 4 = 4;lower limit x = 0 par 0;uttar 4 − 0 = 4. Curve 0 se √{2~3} tak negative rehta hai, uske baad positive.",-1],[2,3,"The work W = ∫₀³ 6x² dx, expressed in joules, equals",["162","54","18","27"],1,"∫ 6x²dx = {6x³~3} = 2x³;limits: 2(3)³ − 2(0)³ = 2 × 27 = 54 J;27 J me coefficient 2 chhoot gaya, 18 J me average-force wali truti aur 162 J me ghaat galat hai.",-1],[3,1,"If log₁₀2 = 0.301, then log₁₀5 equals",["0.5","1.301","0.699","0.301"],2,"5 ko {10~2} roop me likho;bhaag ke niyam se log 10 − log 2 = 1 − 0.301;uttar 0.699 — division, logs ke antar ke barabar hota hai.",-1],[3,2,"If ln x = 3, then the value of x is approximately",["9","3","6.7","20.1"],3,"ln x = 3 ka arth x = e³ (logarithm ki paribhasha);e ≈ 2.718, atah e³ ≈ 2.718 × 2.718 × 2.718 ≈ 20.1;9 ya 3 sochna isliye galat kyunki ln ka aadhar 10 nahi, e hai.",-1],[3,3,"If 3ˣ = 20, then x equals",["{log 20~log 3}","{20~3}","{log 3~log 20}","60"],0,"Donon taraf log lo: x log 3 = log 20;iskar x = {log 20~log 3};values daalo to {1.301~0.477} ≈ 2.73;aadhar same ho to ghaataankon ki tulna seedhi hoti hai;anupat ulta karne par 0.37 aa jaayega.",-1],[3,1,"The expression log a + log b − log c simplifies to",["log ({a~c} + b)","log {ab~c}","log(a + b − c)","log(abc)"],1,"jod gunaa ban jaata hai: log a + log b = log(ab);ghataav bhaag ban jaata hai: log(ab) − log c = log {ab~c};ye niyam keval ek hi aadhar ke logarithms par saath lagu hote hain.",-1],[5,2,"Using the binomial approximation, the value of √1.04 is",["1.002","0.98","1.02","1.04"],2,"1.04 = 1 + 0.04 aur (1 + x)ⁿ ≈ 1 + nx, jo |x| ≪ 1 ke liye maany hai;yahaan n = {1~2}, atah 1 + {1~2} × 0.04 = 1.02;exact √1.04 = 1.0198 — approximation isi ke bahut paas deta hai.",-1],[5,3,"In the expansion of (1 + y)^({1~2}), the term containing y² is",["+{y²~4}","{y²~2}","−{y²~2}","−{y²~8}"],3,"Is pad ka gunaaank {n(n − 1)~2!} hota hai;n = {1~2} rakhne par {(0.5)(−0.5)~2} = −{1~8};atah pad = −{y²~8}. Yeh negative pad batata hai ki 1 + {y~2} thoda adhik value de deta hai.",-1],[5,2,"The Maclaurin series of sin x is",["x − {x³~3!} + {x⁵~5!} − …","1 − {x²~2!} + {x⁴~4!} − …","x + {x³~3!} + {x⁵~5!}","eˣ − e⁻ˣ"],0,"sin x ek odd function hai, isliye keval odd ghaaten aayengi;x = 0 par derivatives ka pattern 1, 0, −1, 0, +1 … hai, nishaan ekantar badalte hain;uttar x − {x³~3!} + {x⁵~5!} − …;dusra option cos x (even function) ka vistar hai.",-1],[5,3,"lim (x→0) {1 − cos x~x²} equals",["2","{1~2}","0","1"],1,"Seedha put karne par {0~0} roop banta hai, atah series istemaal karo;cos x = 1 − {x²~2!} + {x⁴~4!} − …, isse 1 − cos x ≈ {x²~2};limit = {x²~2} ÷ x² → {1~2};L'Hospital niyam se bhi wahi.",-1],[5,2,"lim (x→0) {sin ax~x} equals",["0","{1~a}","a","1"],2,"L'Hospital niyam: numerator ka derivative a cos ax, denominator ka derivative 1;donon par x = 0 rakhne par a cos 0 = a;yehi standard limit {sin ax~ax} → 1 ka dusra roop hai, jo chhote-kon approximation ki bunyaad hai.",-1],[5,3,"The expansion of ln(1 + x), for small values of x, is",["x + {x²~2} + {x³~3}","x − {x²~2} − {x³~3}","1 + x − {x²~2}","x − {x²~2} + {x³~3}"],3,"Pehle jaani hui series: {1~1 + x} = 1 − x + x² − x³ + …;iska 0 se x tak pad-dar-pad integration karo;milta hai x − {x²~2} + {x³~3} − …, jo |x| ke 1 se kam hone par abhisarit hoti hai.",-1],[4,2,"Using the small-angle approximation, the value of sin 2° is",["0.035","0.017","2","0.02"],0,"Sab pehle degrees ko radians me badlo: 2° = {2π~180} = 0.0349 rad;chhote kon ke liye sinθ ≈ θ maan lo;uttar 0.035 — degree me direct approximation lagana niyam-virudh hai.",-1],[4,1,"For a very small angle θ, the quantity tanθ is approximately",["θ²","θ","1","{1~θ}"],1,"tanθ = {sinθ~cosθ} likho;chhote kon par sinθ ≈ θ aur cosθ ≈ 1 − {θ²~2} ≈ 1;anupat keval θ ban jaata hai;yahi approximation lola ka T = 2π√{l~g} nikalne deta hai.",8],[4,1,"One radian, expressed in degrees, is nearly",["90°","3.14°","57.3°","1°"],2,"π rad = 180° (paribhasha se);iskar 1 rad = {180~π} = 57.3°;trikonaamitiyak fhalanon ke derivative aur integral ke sutr tabhi sahi hain jab kon radians me maapa gaya ho.",-1],[6,1,"In T = 2π√{l~g}, if the percentage errors in l and g are 2% and 1%, the maximum percentage error in T is",["3%","2%","0.5%","1.5%"],3,"Truti-prasar: ghaat relative truti ko multiply karta hai;{ΔT~T} = {1~2}{Δl~l} + {1~2}{Δg~g};= {1~2}(2%) + {1~2}(1%) = 1% + 0.5% = 1.5%;constant 2π koi truti nahi deta.",-1],[6,2,"For a density ρ = {m~V} with percentage errors of 2% in mass and 3% in volume, the maximum percentage error in ρ is",["5%","6%","1%","1.5%"],0,"Gunaaank ya bhaag me saapeksh trutiyaan judti hain;{Δρ~ρ} = {Δm~m} + {ΔV~V} = 2% + 3%;uttar 5% — yeh adhikatam seema hai;trutiyaan svatantra (random) hon to √(2² + 3²) ≈ 3.6% lagta.",-1],[7,1,"The area under a velocity–time graph represents",["force","displacement","acceleration","speed"],1,"Paribhasha se: s = ∫ v dt;har patli patti ka kshetraphal v × Δt, unka yog = displacement;usi graph ki slope {dv~dt} tvaran deti hai — kshetraphal aur slope me chunav dhyan se karo.",-1],[8,2,"For x = 2t² − 6t + 4, the acceleration at t = 3 s is",["2 m s⁻²","0","4 m s⁻²","−6 m s⁻²"],2,"v = {dx~dt} = 4t − 6 aur a = {dv~dt} = 4 m s⁻²;yeh samay se mukt hai, atah t = 3 s par bhi 4 m s⁻²;x–t graph parabolik hai yaani tvaran akar; −6 to velocity ka prarambhik gunaaank hai.",-1],[7,2,"As shown in the figure, the work done by the force over the displacement from 0 to 4 m is",["20 J","40 J","16 J","24 J"],3,"W = ∫ F dx = vakra ke neeche ka kshetraphal;yahaan trapezium bana hai (F = 2 N se 10 N tak);kshetraphal = {1~2}(2 + 10)(4) = 24 J;same result ∫₀⁴ (2 + 2x)dx = [2x + x²]₀⁴ = 8 + 16 = 24 J.",0],[7,2,"The slope of the tangent to an x–t graph at a point gives",["instantaneous velocity","average velocity","acceleration","total displacement"],0,"Tangent ki slope = seema me {Δx~Δt} = {dx~dt}, arthaat usi kshn ka velocity;do binduon ko milane wali jya (chord) ki slope ausat velocity deti hai;jahan graph flat hai (ucchisht bindu) vahaan slope zero, atah velocity zero.",2],[7,3,"The slope of the tangent to the curve y = {1~x + a} at x = 0 is",["{1~a}","−{1~a²}","+{1~a²}","−a"],1,"Ghaat −1 me likho: y = (x + a)^(-1);{dy~dx} = −(x + a)^(-2);x = 0 rakhne par −{1~a²}. Curve neeche ki or ja raha hai, isliye slope negative hi aana chahiye.",3],[7,3,"If x varies as t√t, then the velocity varies with time as",["remains constant","∝ {1~√t}","∝ √t","∝ t"],2,"x = kt√t maankar derivative lo: v = {3k~2}√t, yaani v ∝ √t;tvaran a = {dv~dt} = {3k~4√t} — samay ke saath ghat-ta hai;graph ka slope badhta hai par curvature kam hoti jaati hai.",-1],[8,2,"Over one complete cycle, the average value of sin²ωt is",["1","0","{2~π}","{1~2}"],3,"Sarvasmrika: sin²θ = {1 − cos 2θ~2};poore chakron me cos 2ωt ka ausat zero hota hai (samiti se);atah ausat = {1~2};isi liye prityaavarti dhara ki ausat shakti {1~2}i₀²R likhi jaati hai.",-1],[8,1,"For x = t² + 2t in SI units, the velocity at t = 2 s is",["6 m s⁻¹","4 m s⁻¹","8 m s⁻¹","2 m s⁻¹"],0,"Velocity = {dx~dt} = 2t + 2;t = 2 s rakhne par 4 + 2 = 6 m s⁻¹;yahi value x–t graph par usi bindu ki tangent ki slope se bhi padhi ja sakti hai.",-1],[8,3,"A current is 1 A during the first half and 3 A during the second half of a cycle. Its rms value is",["2.5 A","√5 A","2 A","√2 A"],1,"rms ka arth: root of the mean of the squares;square karo: 1² = 1 aur 3² = 9;mean = {1 + 9~2} = 5, atah root = √5 ≈ 2.24 A;saadhaaran ausat 2 A hamesha rms se kam aata hai.",-1],[8,2,"The minimum value of K = 2v² − 8v + 10 is",["2","8","6","10"],2,"Ativyapti ke liye {dK~dv} = 4v − 8 = 0 se v = 2;K(2) = 2(4) − 8(2) + 10 = 8 − 16 + 10 = 6;doosra derivative {d²K~dv²} = +4, yaani dhan, atah yeh bindu nyoontam hai.",-1],[8,2,"For x = 4t − 3t², the velocity becomes zero at the time t equal to",["{4~3} s","1 s","0 s","{2~3} s"],3,"v = {dx~dt} = 4 − 6t;ishe zero ke barabar rakho: 4 − 6t = 0;t = {2~3} s — yahi ucchisht kshn hai, jahan velocity timik roop se zero hoti hai par tvaran −6 m s⁻² bana rehta hai.",-1],[8,3,"A particle starts with u = 10 m s⁻¹ and moves with a = −2 m s⁻². Its displacement is maximum at the time t equal to",["5 s","10 s","2 s","25 s"],0,"Displacement tab adhiktam jab palta hai, arthaat v = 0;v = u + at se 0 = 10 − 2t;iskar t = 5 s;us kshn tak displacement {u²~2a} = 25 m hoga — prashn me samay maanga gaya hai.",-1],[8,2,"A constant force of 10 N acts for 2 s. The change in momentum, in kg m s⁻¹, is",["2","20","5","10"],1,"Aavedya–sanveg pramay: Δp = ∫ F dt;bal akar hai to integral saadhaaran gunaaank ban jaata hai: 10 × 2 = 20;chhota bal lambe samay tak lage to bhi bada sanveg-parivartan mil sakta hai.",-1],[8,2,"For U(x) = 4x² − 8x, the equilibrium position and its nature are",["x = 0, neutral","x = 1, unstable","x = 1, stable","x = 2, unstable"],2,"Bal F = −{dU~dx} = −(8x − 8);samya ke liye F = 0 se x = 1;{d²U~dx²} = +8, yaani dhan, arthaat sthiti-urja nyoontam hai;urja-vakra ka nyoontam bindu sthaayi samya dikhata hai.",5],[8,3,"A sample contains 10⁶ nuclei with a half-life of 10⁵ s. The number of nuclei remaining after 3 × 10⁵ s is",["0.5 × 10⁶","0.25 × 10⁶","2 × 10⁵","0.125 × 10⁶"],3,"Kitne ardh-aayu bate: n = {3 × 10⁵~10⁵} = 3;N = N₀{1~2}ⁿ = {10⁶~2³} = {10⁶~8};uttar 0.125 × 10⁶;N = N₀e^(−λt) me λ = {ln 2~T½} daalne se bhi yahi milta hai.",4],[8,2,"The perpendicular distance of the point (2, 3) from the line 3x + 4y = 12 is",["0","{12~5}","1","5"],0,"Sutra d = {|Ax₀ + By₀ + C|~√(A² + B²)};ansh = |3(2) + 4(3) − 12| = |12 − 12| = 0;atah d = 0 — bindu rekhapar hi sthit hai; aise prashn me yahi pehli janch hai.",-1],[8,2,"The period of small oscillations of a simple pendulum of length 1 m, taking g = 10 m s⁻², is",["6.28 s","2 s","1 s","4 s"],1,"T = 2π√{l~g} = 6.28 × √{1~10};√0.1 ≈ 0.316, atah T ≈ 6.28 × 0.316 ≈ 1.99 ≈ 2 s;yeh sutra keval sinθ ≈ θ wali laghu-ikuti dohon ke liye maany hai.",8],[8,3,"A charge flows with a current i = 2t (in amperes) from t = 0 to t = 3 s. The total charge, in coulombs, is",["3","12","9","6"],2,"i = {dq~dt} se q = ∫ i dt = ∫₀³ 2t dt;antiderivative t², evaluate: 3² − 0 = 9;uttar 9 C;i–t graph ka trikon {1~2} × 3 × 6 = 9 C se turant janch ho jaati hai.",-1],[8,2,"A body starts from rest with an acceleration a = 4t m s⁻². Its velocity at t = 3 s is",["12 m s⁻¹","4 m s⁻¹","36 m s⁻¹","18 m s⁻¹"],3,"dv = a dt integrate karo: v = ∫₀³ 4t dt = [2t²]₀³;= 2(3)² − 0 = 18 m s⁻¹ (v₀ = 0 hone se integration constant zero);a–t graph ka kshetraphal {1~2} × 3 × 12 = 18 se bhi wahi.",-1],[8,3,"If the electric potential is V = {k~r}, then the field E = −{dV~dr} varies with r as",["∝ {1~r²}","∝ {1~r}","∝ r","∝ {1~r³}"],0,"V = k r⁻¹ likho;{dV~dr} = −k r⁻²;E = −{dV~dr} = {k~r²}, arthaat E ∝ {1~r²};negative nishaan keval disha batata hai (jis or potential ghat raha hai).",-1],[8,3,"The moment of inertia of a uniform rod of mass M and length L, about a perpendicular axis through its centre, is",["{ML²~2}","{ML²~12}","{ML²~3}","ML²"],1,"Rekhik ghanta λ = {M~L} aur element dm = λ dx;I = ∫ x²dm = λ{x³~3}, limits −{L~2} se +{L~2};= λ{L³~12} = {ML²~12};axis rod ke sire par se guzre to limits 0 se L aur uttar {ML²~3}.",-1],[8,3,"The volume of a cone of base radius 0.1 m and height 0.3 m, keeping π, is",["0.03π m³","0.0001π m³","0.001π m³","0.003π m³"],2,"Height z par trijya rakheek ghat-ti hai: r(1 − {z~h});disk ka aayatan πr² dz me samakalit karo;V = {πr²h~3} = {π(0.01)(0.3)~3} = 0.001π m³ — same base aur height ke vartul ka ek-tehaai bhaag.",-1],[9,2,"The work done by the force F = 4 − x newtons over the displacement from 0 to 3 m is",["12 J","4.5 J","3 J","7.5 J"],3,"W = ∫₀³ (4 − x)dx = [4x − {x²~2}]₀³;= (12 − 4.5) − 0 = 7.5 J;12 J tab aayega jab bal ko akar 4 N maan liya jaaye;graph ka trapezium {1~2}(4 + 1)(3) = 7.5 se janch karo.",1],[0,2,"A force of 8 N makes an angle of 60° with the x-axis. Its y-component and the value of tanθ are",["4√3 N and √3","4 N and 1","8√3 N and 2","4√3 N and {1~√2}"],0,"Jis axis se kon maapa jaata hai, us ka component cos se milta hai;Fₓ = 8 cos 60° = 4 N aur F_y = 8 sin 60° = 4√3 N;tanθ = {F_y~Fₓ} = {4√3~4} = √3, jo 60° ke saath mel khaata hai.",7],[0,3,"If A = 2î + λĵ and B = 3î − 4ĵ add up to a vector along the x-axis, then λ equals",["0","4","−4","3"],1,"A + B = 5î + (λ − 4)ĵ;x-axis ke anudish ka arth hai ki ĵ ka component zero ho;λ − 4 = 0 se λ = 4 — disha-nibandh ko equation me badalna hi is prashn ki kali hai.",-1],[0,2,"A tangential force of 40 N acts at a distance r = 0.5 m from the axis. The magnitude of the torque is",["80 N m","2 N m","20 N m","0"],2,"Bal-aaghurn τ = rF sinθ, jahaan θ, r aur F ke beech ka kon hai;spurshiya bal ke liye θ = 90° aur sin 90° = 1, yaani aaghurn adhiktam;τ = 0.5 × 40 = 20 N m. Bal trijya ke anudish hota to τ zero.",-1],[0,3,"The angle between the vectors A = î + √3 ĵ and B = î − √3 ĵ is",["60°","90°","150°","120°"],3,"A · B = 1(1) + √3(−√3) = 1 − 3 = −2;|A| = |B| = √(1 + 3) = 2;cosθ = {−2~4} = −{1~2} se θ = 120°;dot product negative ho to kon 90° se adhika hota hai.",-1],[0,3,"A boat moves at 3 m s⁻¹ due north while the current flows at 1 m s⁻¹ due east. Its speed relative to the ground and the angle with the east direction are",["√10, 71.6°","4, 90°","√10, 45°","2, 71.6°"],0,"East = x aur north = y maankar v = 1î + 3ĵ;|v| = √(1² + 3²) = √10 ≈ 3.16 m s⁻¹;kon = tan⁻¹{3~1} = 71.6°;sankhyaon ko seedha jodna (4 m s⁻¹) keval tab sahi hai jab donon ek hi rekha me hon.",-1],[0,2,"Statement 1: for non-zero vectors, A · B = 0 means they are perpendicular. Statement 2: A · B is a scalar. Statement 3: A · B = 0 forces A = 0 or B = 0. The correct statements are",["Only 3","1 and 2","1, 2 and 3","Only 2"],1,"A · B = AB cosθ; non-zero vectors me yeh keval cosθ = 0 se zero hota hai, yaani θ = 90° — Statement 1 sahi;result sankhya aur cosθ ka gunaan hai, koi disha nahi — Statement 2 sahi;beejganit ka ab = 0 wala tark vectors par lagu nahi hota — Statement 3 galat.",-1],[0,3,"From the identity A × (B × C) = B(A · C) − C(A · B), the vector A × (B × C) lies",["always along C","in the plane of A and B","in the plane of B and C","perpendicular to A and outside that plane"],2,"Daayaan paksh αB + βC ke roop me hai, jahaan α = A · C aur β = A · B;B aur C ke aise kisii bhi rekhik snyojan ka vector unhi ke tal me rehta hai;smaran-niyam: BAC − CAB.",-1],[0,2,"The scalar projection of A = 3î + 4ĵ on the direction of B = 5î + 12ĵ is",["{3~5}","5","{63~169}","{63~13}"],3,"Saraksh prakshhep = {A · B~|B|};A · B = 15 + 48 = 63 aur |B| = √(25 + 144) = 13;uttar {63~13} ≈ 4.85;|B| se bhaag karna bhool jaane par 63 mil jaata hai — yahi prachalit truti hai.",7],[0,2,"If A = 2î + ĵ + 3k̂ and B = 4î + λĵ + 6k̂ are parallel, then λ equals",["2","3","6","4"],0,"Samantarata ki shart: components samaanupati hone chahiye;{4~2} = {6~3} = 2, atah {λ~1} = 2 hona chahiye;iskar λ = 2. Doosra tareeka: A × B = 0 se bhi yahi shart milti hai.",-1],[0,3,"For A = î + ĵ + k̂, B = ĵ + k̂ and C = î, the scalar triple product [A B C] equals",["3","0","1","−1"],1,"Yahaan A = B + C, atah teeno vectors ek hi tal me hain (samtliya);samtliya vectors se bana samaantaraaghtak chaptā hota hai, uska aayatan zero;Determinant kholkar: 1(0) − 1(−1) + 1(−1) = 0 ✓.",-1],[0,1,"The cross product î × ĵ equals",["0","î + ĵ","k̂","−k̂"],2,"Right-hand niyam: î se ĵ ki or ungli ghumaao, angootha k̂ dikhayega;chakraakiy kram î → ĵ → k̂ me gunaanhan dhan milta hai;kram badalne par ĵ × î = −k̂, aur ek hi aksh par î × î = 0.",-1],[8,2,"If a = ct and the particle starts from rest, its velocity is",["ct","ct²","{ct²~4}","{ct²~2}"],3,"dv = a dt integrate karo: v = ∫₀ᵗ ct dt = c{t²~2} = {ct²~2};v₀ = 0 hone se integration constant zero;a–t graph ke trikon ka kshetraphal {1~2} · t · (ct) se bhi wahi value milti hai.",-1],[8,2,"The acceleration of a body on a smooth (frictionless) incline of 30°, taking g = 10 m s⁻², is",["5 m s⁻²","10 m s⁻²","8.66 m s⁻²","2.5 m s⁻²"],0,"Gurutvaakarshak bal ka tal ke anudish wala bhaag mg sinθ hota hai;ma = mg sin 30° se a = 10 × 0.5 = 5 m s⁻²;mg cosθ keval abhilamb bal ko santulit karta hai, gati me yogdaan nahi deta.",-1],[8,3,"Using the binomial approximation for L = ∫₀¹ √(1 + 4x²) dx, the value of L is about",["{4~3}","{5~3}","{7~3}","2"],1,"(1 + u)^({1~2}) ≈ 1 + {u~2} lo aur u = 4x² rakho;integrand ≈ 1 + 2x²; iska samakalan: [x + {2x³~3}]₀¹ = 1 + {2~3} = {5~3} ≈ 1.67 m;manyata 4x² ≪ 1 hai, isliye uttar anumaanit roop me liya gaya.",-1],[8,2,"Over half an oscillation, the average magnitude of the restoring force for x = A sin ωt is",["{mω²A~2}","0","{2mω²A~π}","mω²A"],2,"Bal F = mω²A sinωt ka parimaann ausat nikaalna hai;ausat = {ω~π}∫ F dt, limits 0 se {π~ω} tak (ardh-aavart);∫ sinωt dt = {2~ω} rakhne par uttar {2mω²A~π};|sin| ka ausat {2~π} aur sin² ka {1~2} — dono me bhed rakho.",-1],[8,3,"The integral ∫_(1)^(∞) {kq~r²} dr represents",["the average field over the region","zero","the amount of charge","the potential kq at r = 1"],3,"kq∫_(1)^(∞) r⁻²dr = kq[−{1~r}]_(1)^(∞);upper limit par {1~r} → 0 aur lower limit par {1~1} = 1;uttar kq, arthaat V = {kq~r} ka value r = 1 par, kyonki E = −{dV~dr};r → 0 par yeh samakalan apasaari ho jaata hai.",-1],[8,3,"The maximum area of a rectangle whose perimeter is 40 m is",["100 m²","80 m²","200 m²","400 m²"],0,"Bhujaayein x aur 20 − x (kyonki ardh-paridhi 20 m hai);kshetraphal A = x(20 − x);{dA~dx} = 20 − 2x = 0 se x = 10;{d²A~dx²} = −2, yaani negative, atah adhiktam confirm hota hai, atah 100 m² — chaarbetu (square) hi shreshh hai.",-1],[1,3,"If x = a cos ωt and y = a sin ωt, then {dx~dt} equals",["aω c